        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            If you are starting from nothing and your work is framing, demolition, or anything where raw output and North American parts availability matter, DeWalt is the safer commitment. If your days are long, your tools are in your hands continuously, and finish quality matters more than peak torque, Makita is the one you will still be happy with in year five.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Both are genuinely professional platforms and neither is a mistake. The real error is splitting between them — two battery stocks, two chargers, and half the depth in each.
          </p>
